    "result_text": "The full test suite (both tests in `AcceptanceTest`, the only `@Test` class) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a structured address form for owners while keeping the flat `address` fully backward-compatible.\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2192 `OwnerFields`/`Owner` DTOs)**\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` string fields.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list (validity of the two forms is now decided in application logic), so earlier minimal owners and new structured owners are both accepted. `address` is documented as the composed, normalized output.\n\n**Normalization & composition (`NormalizeAddress.java`)** \u2014 the first step of `POST /api/owners`, so its result feeds everything downstream:\n- When a non-blank `addressLine1` is supplied, both lines are normalized (via the existing `AddressNormalizer`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET` etc.) and `address` is composed as the normalized `addressLine1`, plus a single space and the normalized `addressLine2` when present. `addressLine2` is set to null when blank.\n- Otherwise the flat `address` is normalized as before. This means the household hash, postcode validation and locality \u2014 all of which read the request via the published variable \u2014 automatically operate on the structured value when present, falling back to the flat address.\n\n**Validity (`RequireOwnerFields.java`)**: an owner needs an address in *either* form (non-blank `addressLine1` **or** flat `address`), plus city.\n\n**Persistence** so the fields survive create\u2192GET:\n- `Owner` entity gained `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` columns + accessors.\n- Added `address_line1`/`address_line2` columns (at the end of the `owners` table) to all four `schema.sql` files, and appended two trailing NULLs to the positional hsqldb seed inserts (the DB the tests use; h2/postgres seeds use named columns and mysql a different form, so they were unaffected).\n- `ApplyOwner` (the PUT path) now also carries the structured fields.\n\nMapStruct maps the new fields by name automatically, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `addressLine1` (normalized) and the composed `address` \u2014 exactly what the new acceptance test asserts.",
